# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn node1410
node1410 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>ismn</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter &quot;M&quot; for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
